## Homelab layout

- Image: `ghcr.io/serfriz/caddy-duckdns:2` (DuckDNS DNS-01 module).
- **Rootless** quadlet; host ports `8080:80`, `8443:443` with UFW iptables `80→8080`, `443→8443`.
- Config: `/etc/caddy/` (Caddyfile, `sites/`, `snippets/`). Data: `/srv/caddy/` → `/data/` (ACME, logs).
- Podman network: `homelab` — upstreams `vaultwarden:80`, `adguardhome:3000`.
- Sites: `tapocek.duckdns.org`, `adguard-tapocek.duckdns.org` — one file per service in `sites/`, no wildcards.

## Rules

1. Use Caddyfile directives and placeholders from official docs (`{remote_host}`, `{host}`, etc.) — verify placeholder names on the directive page.
2. `reverse_proxy` upstreams: use container names on `homelab` network, not host localhost.
3. Forwarded headers: match [Vaultwarden proxy docs](https://github.com/dani-garcia/vaultwarden/wiki/Configuration-overview#reverse-proxy) when proxying Vaultwarden.
4. New services: add `sites/{name}.caddy`, join `homelab.network`, avoid new host ports when possible.
5. DuckDNS tokens: separate env vars per DuckDNS registration (`DUCKDNS_API_TOKEN`, `DUCKDNS_ADGUARD_API_TOKEN`).

Fetch directive docs when adding unfamiliar blocks — Caddy v2 syntax differs from nginx.
